Job Title: Quality Analyst (Customer Experience Team)

Location: Bangalore, Koramangala. 

Job Type: Full-time

Reports To: Quality Lead

Budget: UPTO 5lpa

Experience: Minimum 2 to 3 years as a Quality Analyst in a customer service environment

(Please don't apply if you don't have relevant experience)

As a Quality Analyst, you will audit customer interactions across voice, chat and ticketing, email channels, &nbsp; 

identify what is going wrong and why, and convert those findings into feedback and coaching that&nbsp; 

measurably improves agent performance. The role carries end-to-end ownership of the quality cycle -

auditing against defined parameters, marking critical errors accurately, delivering structured feedback, &nbsp; 

participating in calibration, identifying training needs and publishing quality reporting. 

You will work closely&nbsp; with the Training team and with Operations, so findings translate into action on the floor rather than sitting&nbsp; in a report. 

Must have: 

- Bachelor's degree or equivalent. • Minimum 2 to 3 years of experience as a Quality Analyst in a customer service, customer support or&nbsp; 

contact centre environment. 

• Hands-on experience auditing interactions across at least one of voice, chat or ticketing, with exposure&nbsp; 

to more than one channel preferred. 

• Working knowledge of quality management or audit tools, and the ability to pick up a new platform&nbsp; 

quickly. 

• Sound understanding of quality parameters, critical error frameworks and audit governance. 

• Practical experience of feedback mechanisms and coaching models, with a track record of feedback&nbsp; 

that changed agent behaviour. Experience of participating in calibration and maintaining scoring consistency. 

• Strong analytical skills and working Excel - pivot tables, lookups and comfort handling large audit data&nbsp; 

sets. 

• Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to write observations a third party can act&nbsp; 

on without further explanation. 

• Objectivity and the confidence to hold a position in a performance conversation, balanced with&nbsp; 

empathy towards agents. 

• Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet audit and reporting deadlines consistently.

