Search is one of the most critical customer-facing capabilities at Tesco, powering the discovery of millions of products across our digital ecosystem. We are on a journey to transform traditional keyword-based search into an intelligent, AI-driven discovery platform that delivers highly relevant, personalized, and conversational experiences for our customers. As part of the Search & Discovery team, you will lead a high-performing group of engineers building and operating large-scale search systems that serve millions of customer interactions daily. Our platform combines traditional information retrieval techniques with cutting-edge machine learning, semantic search, hybrid retrieval, ranking optimization, and conversational AI experiences. You will work at the intersection of distributed systems, search relevance, machine learning, and customer experience, helping shape the future of how customers discover products across Tesco. 

You will be responsible for
You Will Be Responsible ForAs a Software Development Manager within the Search & Discovery organization, your primary responsibility will be to build and lead a highly engaged team of search engineers while delivering world-class search experiences for Tesco customers. You will balance people leadership, technical strategy, and delivery execution, helping the team solve complex problems spanning retrieval, ranking, relevance, personalization, and AI-powered search capabilities. People Leadership• Build, coach, and develop a team of talented software engineers and senior engineers. • Create a culture of ownership, innovation, inclusion, and continuous learning. • Support career growth through mentoring, coaching, regular feedback, and development planning. • Drive high standards of engineering excellence, accountability, and quality. • Actively participate in hiring and help build diverse, high-performing engineering teams. Technical Leadership• Partner with Principal Engineers, Product Managers, and Data Scientists to define and execute the Search technology strategy. • Guide architectural decisions across search, retrieval, ranking, indexing, and AI-driven discovery systems. • Drive adoption of modern search technologies including semantic retrieval, vector search, hybrid ranking, and conversational AI capabilities. • Stay close to the technology and provide technical guidance without becoming a bottleneck. • Champion engineering best practices around scalability, resilience, observability, security, and performance. ________________________________________Experience Relevant for the Role• Proven experience managing software engineering teams delivering complex distributed systems in production environments. • Strong experience leading backend engineering teams working with Java-based technology stacks. • Hands-on experience building and operating large-scale search platforms using Elasticsearch or similar search technologies. • Experience delivering highly scalable and resilient customer-facing services. • Experience working in Agile product development environments. • Experience partnering with Product Management and senior stakeholders to define priorities and roadmaps. • Experience managing globally distributed engineering teams is desirable. • Exposure to machine learning, information retrieval, ranking systems, recommendation systems, or applied AI is advantageous. 

You will need
Technical SkillsSearch & Discovery• Deep understanding of modern search architectures and information retrieval concepts. • Experience with Elasticsearch indexing, querying, relevance tuning, and performance optimization. • Knowledge of semantic search, vector embeddings, hybrid retrieval, and ranking systems. • Familiarity with search quality metrics, experimentation frameworks, and relevance evaluation techniques. • Understanding of conversational search, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and AI-powered discovery systems is highly desirable. Software Engineering• Strong foundation in Java and distributed systems design. • Experience with cloud-native architectures and microservices. • Experience with event-driven architectures and messaging systems such as Kafka. • Strong understanding of performance, scalability, reliability, and operational excellence. • Experience with observability, incident management, and production support. 

